WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.050
A volunteer sits down.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.130
"Today," says the researcher,
"we're testing your memory."

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.110
But the researcher's
notebook says something else.

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.830
The study is really about
something she hasn't been told.

5
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.180
And behind a one-way mirror, someone
is quietly watching her every move.

6
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.440
Psychologists have misled
participants like this.

7
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.970
Is that ever allowed?

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.710
And if so, when?

9
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.550
In this mission, you'll meet the
rules UK psychologists follow,

10
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.140
from the British Psychological Society.

11
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.260
You'll find out what informed
consent and deception really mean.

12
00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:39.240
And you'll see why participants should
leave a study in the same state as they

13
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.440
arrived.

14
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:46.030
Your mission: decide when, if ever,
it's acceptable to deceive participants.
